  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"838\" data-end=\"965\">\n<p data-start=\"840\" data-end=\"875\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong data-start=\"840\" data-end=\"873\">Normal / Background Exposure:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"878\" data-end=\"965\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\" data-start=\"878\" data-end=\"913\">\n<p data-start=\"880\" data-end=\"913\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Mercury &lt;10 &micro;g/L in spot urine.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\" data-start=\"916\" data-end=\"965\">\n<p data-start=\"918\" data-end=\"965\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Typically reflects <strong data-start=\"937\" data-end=\"964\">no significant exposure</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\" data-start=\"967\" data-end=\"1243\">\n<p data-start=\"969\" data-end=\"999\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong data-start=\"969\" data-end=\"997\">Elevated Mercury Levels:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1002\" data-end=\"1243\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\" data-start=\"1002\" data-end=\"1108\">\n<p data-start=\"1004\" data-end=\"1108\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong data-start=\"1004\" data-end=\"1019\">10&ndash;50 &micro;g/L:</strong> May indicate <strong data-start=\"1033\" data-end=\"1075\">occupational or environmental exposure</strong> &ndash; clinical correlation needed.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\" data-start=\"1111\" data-end=\"1243\">\n<p data-start=\"1113\" data-end=\"1243\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong data-start=\"1113\" data-end=\"1126\">&gt;50 &micro;g/L:</strong> Suggestive of <strong data-start=\"1141\" data-end=\"1177\">significant exposure or toxicity</strong>; consider <strong data-start=\"1188\" data-end=\"1216\">24-hour urine collection</strong> and clinical evaluation.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\" data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1366\">\n<p data-start=\"1247\" data-end=\"1275\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong data-start=\"1247\" data-end=\"1273\">Creatinine Correction:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1278\" data-end=\"1366\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\" data-start=\"1278\" data-end=\"1366\">\n<p data-start=\"1280\" data-end=\"1366\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Ensures accuracy by accounting for urine dilution; values reported as &micro;g/g creatinine.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\" data-start=\"1368\" data-end=\"1487\">\n<p data-start=\"1370\" data-end=\"1487\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Should be correlated with <strong data-start=\"1396\" data-end=\"1486\">clinical symptoms (neuro, renal, GI), exposure history, and other heavy metals testing</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
